{{- /*
=============================================================================
configure-pi-external-editor — idempotent ~/.pi/agent/settings.json externalEditor patcher

Pi (the @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent open-source AI coding harness) reads
its external editor selection from ~/.pi/agent/settings.json's `externalEditor`
key. That file is NOT fully owned by the repo — pi writes runtime keys
(defaultProvider, defaultModel, defaultThinkingLevel, lastChangelogVersion)
and the user edits it interactively via /settings. A templated file target
would clobber those keys; this jq merge preserves every existing field and
only sets the `externalEditor` scalar to `nvim` (the neovim binary installed
as a brew formula in packages.brew.dev).

Uses `run_onchange_before_` semantics:
  • `onchange_` runs only when THIS SCRIPT'S source content has changed
    (chezmoi state hash), so re-applies don't churn ~/.pi/agent/settings.json's
    mtime once the patch is stable.
  • `before_` runs during step 4 of the application order, before file
    targets are written — matters because ~/.pi/agent/settings.json is NOT
    a chezmoi-managed file; this script (alongside the theme and packages
    scripts) is the only writer for the `externalEditor` key.

No-op on a fresh machine where pi has never been run (the ~/.pi/agent/ dir
won't exist yet — pi creates it on first launch). The user runs `pi` once to
initialize, then re-runs `chezmoi apply` to set the external editor. This is
the same friendly-fail-mode pattern AGENTS.md describes for dot_zprofile and
for the other configure-pi-* scripts on a machine where pi isn't initialized.
=============================================================================
*/ -}}
{{- if eq .chezmoi.os "darwin" -}}
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail

PI_DIR="$HOME/.pi/agent"
SETTINGS_FILE="$PI_DIR/settings.json"

# No-op if pi has never been run (dir or settings file doesn't exist).
if [ ! -f "$SETTINGS_FILE" ]; then
  echo "==> Pi settings not found at $SETTINGS_FILE — pi not initialized yet."
  echo "    Run 'pi' once to initialize, then re-run 'chezmoi apply' to set the external editor."
  exit 0
fi

echo "==> Setting external editor to nvim for pi (~/.pi/agent/settings.json)..."
tmp=$(mktemp)
jq --arg editor "nvim" '.externalEditor = $editor' "$SETTINGS_FILE" > "$tmp" && mv "$tmp" "$SETTINGS_FILE"
echo "    externalEditor = nvim (other keys preserved)"
{{- else -}}
{{- /* No-op on non-macOS. */ -}}
{{- end -}}